  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Why one registry rather than three",
      "items": [
        "The three callers want different shapes: a JSON schema, a prompt, and a Kotlin service",
        "Defining a tool once means a hook cannot be callable from cloud Gemini but missing on device",
        "execute() is the same function in all three paths, so a tool behaves identically wherever it is invoked"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "What differs between them",
      "items": [
        "Cloud returns functionCalls[] the SDK dispatches; Nano returns structured output you parse",
        "AppFunctions is invoked by the system Gemini app, so it runs without your UI in the foreground",
        "Only the cloud path does multi-step chains without you writing the loop"
      ]
    }
  ]
